# Moving the caret. Every case runs in Plain Text, Markdown and HTML unless it says otherwise.
# The body is "text:", the caret is put with "caret:", and after "keys:" the caret must be where
# "caret-is:" says.

== Right moves one character
text: one two three
caret: before "two"
keys: {RIGHT}
caret-is: after "one t"

== Left moves one character
text: one two three
caret: before "two"
keys: {LEFT}
caret-is: after "one"

== Ctrl+Right moves to the start of the next word
text: one two three
caret: before "one"
keys: ^{RIGHT}
caret-is: before "two"

== Ctrl+Right twice moves two words
text: one two three
caret: before "one"
keys: ^{RIGHT}^{RIGHT}
caret-is: before "three"

== Ctrl+Left moves to the start of the word the caret is in
text: one two three
caret: after "two th"
keys: ^{LEFT}
caret-is: before "three"

== Ctrl+Left at the start of a word moves to the previous word
text: one two three
caret: before "three"
keys: ^{LEFT}
caret-is: before "two"

== Home moves to the start of the line
text: one two three
caret: before "three"
keys: {HOME}
caret-is: start

== End moves to the end of the line
text: one two three
caret: before "two"
keys: {END}
caret-is: end

== End on the first of two lines stays on that line
text: alpha beta\ngamma delta
caret: before "beta"
keys: {END}
caret-is: after "alpha beta"

== Home on the second of two lines stays on that line
text: alpha beta\ngamma delta
caret: before "delta"
keys: {HOME}
caret-is: before "gamma"

== Down moves to the next line
text: alpha\nbeta\ngamma
caret: start
keys: {DOWN}
caret-is: before "beta"

== Up moves to the previous line
text: alpha\nbeta\ngamma
caret: before "gamma"
keys: {UP}
caret-is: before "beta"

== Down from a long line onto a short one goes to the short line's end
text: a much longer line\nshort\nlast
caret: after "a much longer"
keys: {DOWN}
caret-is: after "short"

== Down through a blank line stops on the blank line
text: alpha\n\ngamma
caret: start
keys: {DOWN}
caret-is: after "alpha\n"

== Ctrl+Home moves to the start of the body
text: alpha\nbeta\ngamma
caret: before "gamma"
keys: ^{HOME}
caret-is: start

== Ctrl+End moves to the end of the body
text: alpha\nbeta\ngamma
caret: before "beta"
keys: ^{END}
caret-is: end

== Ctrl+Down moves to the start of the next paragraph
text: alpha one\nbeta two\ngamma three
caret: after "alpha"
keys: ^{DOWN}
caret-is: before "beta"

== Ctrl+Down twice moves two paragraphs
text: alpha one\nbeta two\ngamma three
caret: start
keys: ^{DOWN}^{DOWN}
caret-is: before "gamma"

== Ctrl+Up inside a paragraph moves to its start
text: alpha one\nbeta two\ngamma three
caret: after "beta"
keys: ^{UP}
caret-is: before "beta"

== Ctrl+Up at the start of a paragraph moves to the previous paragraph
text: alpha one\nbeta two\ngamma three
caret: before "gamma"
keys: ^{UP}
caret-is: before "beta"

== Ctrl+Down on the last paragraph
judgment: On the last paragraph, should Ctrl+Down go to the end of the body (as here) or stay put?
text: alpha one\nbeta two
caret: before "beta"
keys: ^{DOWN}
caret-is: end

== Ctrl+Up on the first paragraph at its start stays put
text: alpha one\nbeta two
caret: start
keys: ^{UP}
caret-is: start

== Page Down in a short body moves to the last line
judgment: In a body shorter than a page, Page Down lands on the last line, keeping the column. Right?
text: alpha\nbeta\ngamma
caret: start
keys: {PGDN}
caret-is: before "gamma"

== Page Up in a short body moves to the first line
text: alpha\nbeta\ngamma
caret: before "gamma"
keys: {PGUP}
caret-is: start
